n:
This section includes eight metaphors, each showing from a different angle the certainty of Jerusalem's upcoming judgment. The images are of: 

- a worthless vine ({{Ezekiel 15:1-8|Ezekiel 15}});

- a faithless wife ({{Ezekiel 16:1-63|Ezekiel 16}});

- a vine and two eagles ({{Ezekiel 17:1-24|Ezekiel 17}});

- Sour grapes ({{Ezekiel 18:1-32|Ezekiel 18}});

- a lion and her cubs ({{Ezekiel 19:1-14|Ezekiel 19}});

- a sword ({{Ezekiel 21:1-32|Ezekiel 21}});

- two corrupt sisters ({{Ezekiel 23:1-49|Ezekiel 23}}); and

- a cooking pot ({{Ezekiel 24:1-27|Ezekiel 24}}).
